== Knowledge continuum ==

BITwiki is the durable semantic knowledge layer. BIThub is the live collaboration/work layer. BITCORE is the cognition and orchestration layer.

<pre>
question / task / signal
→ BIThub discussion + work
→ BITCORE research / synthesis / validation
→ reusable artifact
→ review / correction / provenance
→ BITwiki durable knowledge
→ future retrieval and work
↺
</pre>

'''Useful intelligence should compound.'''

== Working principles ==

* '''Storage saves data. Memory preserves useful context.'''
* '''The map is not the territory, but the map must be clean in order to be able to traverse it.'''
* '''Evidence is signal, not truth.'''
* '''Modularity does not mean fragmentation.'''
* '''Do not consume passively. Generate Signal.'''

== Notice ==

'''Living corpus:''' BITwiki contains human-assisted AI material, historical experimental work, and evolving knowledge. Important claims should be checked against their sources and epistemic context.

V2 is built source-first from the independently verified current-public V1 archive. Historical branches remain traceable; enhancement should preserve the mind of the work while refactoring the machinery around it.

